clearData [SimTalk]
Deletes the dialog items of the Dialog designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.clearData
Example
MyDialog.clearData
clearData [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-5095
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

close [SimTalk] - Dialog
Closes the dialog box of the Dialog designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.close(OK:boolean)
Parameter
The parameter OK of data type boolean designates the action which the dialog takes, OK or Cancel.
Specify true to apply the changes the user made.
Specify false to cancel all changes.
Example
MyDialog.close(true)
SimTalk
open [SimTalk] - Dialog
See also
Show Dialog [Dialog]
close [SimTalk] - Dialog
11-5096 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

closeDialog [SimTalk] - Dialog
Closes the dialog box of the Dialog designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.closeDialog([ApplyChanges:boolean:=true]) → boolean
Parameter
The optional parameter ApplyChanges of data type boolean determines if Plant Simulation ignores all
changes the user made in the dialog or if it accepts and applies these changes.
Specify true to make the Dialog evaluate all settings in the dialog box and apply them as the new values.
Specify false to make the Dialog discards the changes.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is true.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyDialog.closeDialog(true)
SimTalk
openDialog [SimTalk] - Dialog
See also
Show Dialog [Dialog]
closeDialog [SimTalk] - Dialog
Plant Simulation Help 11-5097
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

createButton [SimTalk]
Creates a Button in the Dialog designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createButton(Name:string, X:integer, Y:integer, Width:integer[, 
Parent:string]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Name of data type string designates the Name of the button.
Note
You can set the Caption of the button with the method setCaption.
• The parameter X of data type integer designates the position of the button on the X-axis in the Dialog.
• The parameter Y of data type integer designates the position of the button on the Y-axis in the Dialog.
• The parameter Width of data type integer designates the Width of the button.
• The optional parameter Parent of data type string designates the parent of the drop-down list box, for
example a Group Box or Tab Page.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyTabbedDialog.createButton("Order", 7, 7, 18, "MyTab4")
See also
New Button
