createDropDownListBox [SimTalk]
Creates a Drop-Down List Box in the Dialog designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createDropDownListBox(Name:string, X:integer, Y:integer, 
Width:integer[, Parent:string]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Name of data type string designates the Name of the drop down list box.
• The parameter X of data type integer designates the position of the drop- down list box on the X-Axis in
the Dialog.
• The parameter Y of data type integer designates the position of the drop- down list box on the Y-Axis in
the Dialog.
• The parameter Width of data type integer designates the Width of the drop down list box.
• The optional parameter Parent of data type string designates the parent of the drop-down list box, for
example a Group Box or Tab Page.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyDialog.createDropDownListBox("unit", 12, 1, 10, "Page.Group")
units.create
