createRadioButton [SimTalk]
Creates a Radio Button in the Dialog designated by <Path>.
Remarks
You have to create all items of a group of radio buttons sequentially because Plant Simulation creates the
items according to their row and column position. You cannot arrange two sets of radio buttons as shown
below, where the radio buttons Red and Blue on the left-hand side and the radio buttons Round and
Square on the right-hand side form a group each. Windows ignores the Group ID you enter and groups
the radio buttons row by row according to the Y-coordinate, i.e., it treats Red and Round as one group and
Blue and Square as the other group.
createRadioButton [SimTalk]
11-5108 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If you want to model like this, do not place the radio buttons loosely onto the dialog, but group them
within group boxes.
createRadioButton [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-5109
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createRadioButton(Name:string, X:integer, Y:integer[, 
Parent:string]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter Name of data type string designates the Name of the radio button.
Note
You can set the Caption of the radio button with the method setCaption.
• The parameter X of data type integer designates the position of the radio button on the X-Axis in the
Dialog.
• The parameter Y of data type integer designates the position of the radio button on the Y-Axis in the
Dialog.
• The optional parameter Parent of data type string designates the parent of the radio button, for example
a Group Box or a Tab Page.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MySimpleDialog.createRadioButton("Frontwheel", 3, 0)
