getIndex [SimTalk]
Returns the number of the designated dialog item in the Dialog designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getIndex(DialogItem:string) → integer
Parameter
The parameter DialogItem of data type string designates the List Box, the Drop-Down List Box, or the Tab
Page. The leftmost tab has the number 1.
If you assign another list, and if it is possible, the Dialog selects the item at the same position in the list
box.
If you assign another list, and it is not possible to select the same position in the list box that the previous
selection had, the Dialog automatically selects the first item in the new list.
getIndex [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-5117
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
Is 0 if the drop-down list box does not contain any items.
Is 1 if it does contain items, and no item is selected. Then the Dialog automatically selects the first item in
the list.
Example
print MyDialog.getIndex("doors")
print MyDialog.getIndex("units")
SimTalk
setIndex [SimTalk]
See also
Position of the item in the Items [Dialog] list
getIndex [SimTalk]
11-5118 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

